# YouTube Source Remover

`index.js` is a Tampermonkey userscript for YouTube that patches the built-in share dialog behavior so copied links no longer include the `si` tracking parameter.

## What it does

- Matches all YouTube pages (`www.youtube.com`, `m.youtube.com`, `music.youtube.com`) so the script can stay active across SPA navigation.
- Watches for YouTube’s `yt-copy-link-renderer` share dialog.
- Updates the share input value in `input#share-url` to remove the `si` query parameter.
- Patches the native `#copy-button` click behavior to copy the cleaned URL.
- Falls back to YouTube’s original handler if clipboard access is blocked.

## Why it exists

This script makes shared YouTube links cleaner and more privacy-friendly by stripping the `si` parameter before copying. It also keeps the script active across internal YouTube navigation, which is important because YouTube is a single-page application.

## Notes

- The script uses a `MutationObserver` to detect the share dialog when it appears.
- It also listens for route-change events like `yt-navigate-finish`, `popstate`, and `hashchange`.
- The visible button text is updated to `Anti-Track Copy`.
